WEBVTT

1
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.833
<b>In chapter 5,</b>

2
00:00:47.833 --> 00:00:54.000
<b>Lord Krishna has been explaining to Arjuna about </b>
<b>renunciation and the yoga of action.</b>

3
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.666
<b>In verses 4 and 5 of chapter 5, Lord Krishna </b>
<b>analyzes this and states</b>

4
00:01:00.666 --> 00:01:05.250
<b>that the wise see no difference </b>
<b>between Sankhya and Karma Yoga.</b>

5
00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.416
<b>Sankhya means the path of </b>
<b>renunciation and knowledge,</b>

6
00:01:08.416 --> 00:01:12.125
<b>and Karma Yoga means the path of action.</b>

7
00:01:12.125 --> 00:01:16.000
<b>In these two verses, Lord Krishna explains</b>

8
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.666
<b>that the supreme goal can be </b>
<b>attained through both paths,</b>

9
00:01:19.666 --> 00:01:26.541
<b>which is why the wise see </b>
<b>Sankhya and Karma Yoga as equal.</b>

10
00:01:30.875 --> 00:01:32.583
<b>Lord Krishna says that</b>

11
00:01:32.583 --> 00:01:38.291
<b>only the ignorant see distinction </b>
<b>between Sankhya and Karma Yoga;</b>

12
00:01:38.291 --> 00:01:42.833
<b>in reality, both paths lead to the supreme goal.</b>

13
00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:46.083
<b>When the purpose and goal </b>
<b>of both paths are the same,</b>

14
00:01:46.083 --> 00:01:49.041
<b>should they not be considered equal?</b>

15
00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:53.041
<b>The main point that Lord Krishna </b>
<b>emphasizes is that</b>

16
00:01:53.041 --> 00:01:56.000
<b>through either means, any person</b>

17
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:02.375
<b>can break their material bonds and </b>
<b>attain the state of self-realization.</b>

18
00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:07.083
<b>In Sankhya, if one seeks spiritual </b>
<b>liberation through knowledge,</b>

19
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:12.250
<b>they must first attain freedom from </b>
<b>the desires and wants of this world.</b>

20
00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:13.875
<b>And in Karma Yoga,</b>

21
00:02:13.875 --> 00:02:20.375
<b>if that same person performs their duty </b>
<b>without attachment to the fruits of their actions,</b>

22
00:02:20.375 --> 00:02:23.625
<b>not getting entangled in the bonds of karma,</b>

23
00:02:23.625 --> 00:02:26.958
<b>they too will attain spiritual progress.</b>

24
00:02:26.958 --> 00:02:27.958
<b>However,</b>

25
00:02:27.958 --> 00:02:30.041
<b>while stating that both are equal,</b>

26
00:02:30.041 --> 00:02:36.500
<b>in a very subtle way, Lord Krishna is guiding </b>
<b>Arjuna towards Karma Yoga.</b>

27
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.375
<b>Because</b>

28
00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:43.166
<b>Karma Yoga is not only simple and easy, </b>
<b>but also practical.</b>

29
00:02:43.166 --> 00:02:46.166
<b>The discerning individual </b>
<b>considers selfless Karma Yoga</b>

30
00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:49.958
<b>and the knowledge obtained</b>
<b>from Sankhya as one,</b>

31
00:02:49.958 --> 00:02:55.875
<b>and knows that both paths </b>
<b>fulfill spiritual objectives</b>

32
00:02:55.875 --> 00:03:01.041
<b>and ultimately lead to freedom </b>
<b>from the bonds of karma.</b>

33
00:03:01.666 --> 00:03:05.833


34
00:03:05.833 --> 00:03:14.583
<b>Do you also get confused like Arjuna </b>
<b>about which path to choose in life?</b>

35
00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:17.000
<b>There are countless paths,</b>

36
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:28.833
<b>and it is natural to have preconceived </b>
<b>notions about whether a path is right or wrong.</b>

37
00:03:28.833 --> 00:03:31.541
<b>But true knowledge is gained</b>

38
00:03:31.541 --> 00:03:38.958
<b>only when you recognize the truth behind that</b>
<b>path, abandoning such preconceived notions.</b>

39
00:03:38.958 --> 00:03:44.416
<b>Whether it's peace, progress, </b>
<b>or fulfillment of any goal,</b>

40
00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:51.000
<b>different individuals choose different </b>
<b>paths for similar objectives.</b>

41
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.166
<b>Some choose the path of selfless Karma Yoga,</b>

42
00:03:54.166 --> 00:03:57.916
<b>not getting attached to the fruits of their actions.</b>

43
00:03:57.916 --> 00:04:02.750
<b>While another may choose thepath</b>
<b>of knowledge and analysis.</b>

44
00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:10.250
<b>Outwardly, these paths may seem different, </b>
<b>but inwardly they are the same.</b>

45
00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:17.708
<b>So there is absolutely no need for</b>
<b>you to criticize the path chosen by another.</b>

46
00:04:17.708 --> 00:04:23.333
<b>Know the truth and purpose </b>
<b>behind choosing that path.</b>

47
00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:24.875
<b>By doing so,</b>

48
00:04:24.875 --> 00:04:29.916
<b>you become aware of life's infinite diversities</b>

49
00:04:29.916 --> 00:04:35.458
<b>and understand that every</b>
<b>path has its own significance.</b>

50
00:04:35.458 --> 00:04:38.125
<b>In such a situation, you are free</b>

51
00:04:38.125 --> 00:04:42.708
<b>and able to choose the path suitable for you.</b>

52
00:04:42.708 --> 00:04:44.166
<b>In this way,</b>

53
00:04:44.166 --> 00:04:48.583
<b>you support the path chosen by others</b>

54
00:04:48.583 --> 00:04:55.791
<b>and also confidently move </b>
<b>forward on the path you have chosen.</b>

55
00:04:55.791 --> 00:05:03.416
<b>Rising above the apparent differences, you </b>
<b>become acquainted with the truth of every path</b>

56
00:05:03.416 --> 00:05:14.000
<b>and realize that it is this truth that leads </b>
<b>you and everyone to progress and fulfillment.</b>

57
00:05:14.541 --> 00:05:18.375


58
00:05:18.375 --> 00:05:25.458
<b>Can the preferences of a grandfather </b>
<b>and grandson ever be the same?</b>

59
00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:26.958
<b>The grandfather wants</b>

60
00:05:26.958 --> 00:05:35.041
<b>the grandson to focus on studies and based on </b>
<b>good marks in exams, choose his profession.</b>

61
00:05:35.041 --> 00:05:36.333
<b>On the other hand,</b>

62
00:05:36.333 --> 00:05:39.000
<b>the modern grandson wants to spend time</b>

63
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:48.833
<b>in his extra-curricular activities, such as </b>
<b>sports, painting or music, along with studies.</b>

64
00:05:48.833 --> 00:05:53.208
<b>Who among the two is right?</b>

65
00:05:53.208 --> 00:06:01.000
<b>On most subjects, you may find these two </b>
<b>generations going in opposite directions.</b>

66
00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:05.750
<b>When many generations live </b>
<b>together under one roof,</b>

67
00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:09.916
<b>differences in opinion are natural</b>

68
00:06:09.916 --> 00:06:12.416
<b>and common.</b>

69
00:06:12.416 --> 00:06:14.375
<b>For instance,</b>

70
00:06:14.375 --> 00:06:18.833
<b>the mother-in-law's method </b>
<b>of cooking may be traditional,</b>

71
00:06:18.833 --> 00:06:19.916
<b>but</b>

72
00:06:19.916 --> 00:06:25.791
<b>the younger daughter-in-law wants to </b>
<b>cook only with her modern methods.</b>

73
00:06:25.791 --> 00:06:29.791
<b>Here, the goal of both is the same,</b>

74
00:06:29.791 --> 00:06:35.208
<b>that the family members get </b>
<b>tasty and nutritious food.</b>

75
00:06:35.208 --> 00:06:38.458
<b>What to do when the goal</b>
<b>is the same in the family,</b>

76
00:06:38.458 --> 00:06:43.625
<b>but the paths are different </b>
<b>due to differences of opinion?</b>

77
00:06:43.625 --> 00:06:46.375
<b>what is to be done?</b>

78
00:06:46.375 --> 00:06:59.583
<b>Respect each other's views and give up your </b>
<b>critical prejudices, that is, preconceived notions.</b>

79
00:06:59.583 --> 00:07:02.750
<b>The young should never think</b>

80
00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:06.541
<b>that the elders do not understand today's times,</b>

81
00:07:06.541 --> 00:07:08.541
<b>so they know nothing,</b>

82
00:07:08.541 --> 00:07:10.541
<b>while on the other hand,</b>

83
00:07:10.541 --> 00:07:15.708
<b>the elders should also not consider </b>
<b>the new enthusiasm of the youth as worthless.</b>

84
00:07:15.708 --> 00:07:23.416
<b>If every generation in the house has </b>
<b>a feeling of mutual respect for each other,</b>

85
00:07:23.416 --> 00:07:30.583
<b>then harmony is possible </b>
<b>even with inconsistency in ideas.</b>

86
00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:32.875
<b>I would even say</b>

87
00:07:32.875 --> 00:07:40.666
<b>that these different perspectives </b>
<b>can be helpful in family progress.</b>

88
00:07:45.291 --> 00:07:47.541
<b>In any organization,</b>

89
00:07:47.541 --> 00:07:49.958
<b>the group of colleagues</b>

90
00:07:49.958 --> 00:07:53.750
<b>comes with their unique backgrounds.</b>

91
00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.416
<b>Everyone's thinking is different,</b>

92
00:07:55.416 --> 00:07:57.750
<b>everyone's ideas are different.</b>

93
00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:04.291
<b>So how does the chief executive lead </b>
<b>everyone together in such a situation?</b>

94
00:08:04.291 --> 00:08:09.333
<b>Only a change in perspective is needed,</b>

95
00:08:09.333 --> 00:08:14.541
<b>the scene in front appears in its new form.</b>

96
00:08:14.541 --> 00:08:21.000
<b>The diversity of ideas may </b>
<b>seem like a problem,</b>

97
00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.000
<b>but</b>

98
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:28.375
<b>for an experienced executive, </b>
<b>it proves to be a strength.</b>

99
00:08:28.375 --> 00:08:29.958
<b>Consider this,</b>

100
00:08:29.958 --> 00:08:36.083
<b>different professionals with diverse </b>
<b>backgrounds are working on a single project.</b>

101
00:08:36.083 --> 00:08:39.291
<b>Everyone's ideas and </b>
<b>characteristics are different.</b>

102
00:08:39.291 --> 00:08:40.708
<b>There is a member who</b>

103
00:08:40.708 --> 00:08:47.458
<b>expands each aspect of the project </b>
<b>and looks at it from a micro perspective.</b>

104
00:08:47.458 --> 00:08:53.458
<b>But another believes in analysis and research;</b>

105
00:08:53.458 --> 00:08:56.333
<b>and the third one is practical,</b>

106
00:08:56.333 --> 00:09:01.458
<b>so is in favor of making decisions </b>
<b>only after testing on the ground.</b>

107
00:09:01.458 --> 00:09:03.750
<b>All three approaches can be excellent,</b>

108
00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:09.125
<b>the chief executive can decide </b>
<b>to choose one of the three.</b>

109
00:09:09.125 --> 00:09:10.958
<b>However,</b>

110
00:09:10.958 --> 00:09:16.458
<b>an experienced executive, </b>
<b>while giving due respect to all three,</b>

111
00:09:16.458 --> 00:09:20.166
<b>encompassing all three thought processes,</b>

112
00:09:20.166 --> 00:09:26.541
<b>will create a framework in which </b>
<b>all three aspects are included.</b>

113
00:09:26.541 --> 00:09:29.208
<b>The main thing is just one –</b>

114
00:09:29.208 --> 00:09:35.708
<b>that this new framework is in harmony </b>
<b>with the main objective of the organization.</b>

115
00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:39.083
<b>Will not the merits of these diverse styles,</b>

116
00:09:39.083 --> 00:09:45.750
<b>while strengthening the main objective </b>
<b>of the organization, attain progress?</b>

117
00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.208
<b>Certainly they will.</b>

118
00:09:47.208 --> 00:09:54.375
<b>Senior members have to accept the </b>
<b>ideas of young colleagues with due respect,</b>

119
00:09:54.375 --> 00:09:55.791
<b>and on the other hand,</b>

120
00:09:55.791 --> 00:09:57.416
<b>young colleagues</b>

121
00:09:57.416 --> 00:10:04.958
<b>have to give the same mutual respect to the </b>
<b>decisions and directives taken by the executives.</b>

122
00:10:04.958 --> 00:10:09.625
<b>The job of the executives is to unite diverse ideas,</b>

123
00:10:09.625 --> 00:10:12.416
<b>and the duty of the colleagues</b>

124
00:10:12.416 --> 00:10:17.583
<b>is to show their full dedication </b>
<b>to the decision taken.</b>

